      "title": "Note: Model links",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen-Image 2.1 - BFS Character (Head) Swap\n\nThis is the Qwen-Image 2.1 image-edit workflow set up for **BFS - Best Face Swap** by **Alissonerdx**. Load a **body/base image** (image_1) and a **head/face reference** (image_2), and the LoRA transfers the face and hair from image_2 onto the person in image_1 far more consistently than a plain edit prompt.\n\nNothing extra is needed to use it in your own workflow: just load a BFS LoRA in the LoRA loader and use the swap prompt below.\n\n### BFS LoRA (pick one - try both)\nTwo head-swap LoRAs for Qwen 2.1. v1.1 alternative is the more recent one and is marked recommended, but results vary by image - test both:\n- [bfs_head_v1.1_alternative_qwen_2.1.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Alissonerdx/BFS-Best-Face-Swap/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (loaded here)\n- [bfs_head_v1_qwen_2.1.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Alissonerdx/BFS-Best-Face-Swap/tree/main) -> `models/loras/`\n\nStart at LoRA **strength 1.0**, then adjust for your base model, resolution, and reference image. Input order matters: **body first (image_1), face reference second (image_2).**\n\n### Swap prompt (in the text encode node)\n`head_swap: start with <image1> as the base image, keeping its lighting, environment, and background. remove the head from <image1> completely and replace it with the head from <image2>, strictly preserving the hair, eye color, nose structure from <image2>. copy the direction of the eye, head rotation, micro expressions from <image1>, high quality, sharp details, 4k`\n\n### IMPORTANT - Qwen 2.1 caveat (from the author)\n\"There's a really annoying effect in Qwen 2.1 where even if you change a small part of the image, it seems like the whole image is affected; the colors change, the details are lost, it looks more blurry, etc. The way I managed to mitigate it a bit was by generating the images in 2K, and even then it's still bad.\"\nSo this workflow runs the ResolutionSelector at **2 MP (2K)** to reduce that whole-image drift. Keep it at 2K for the best preservation.\n\n### About this workflow's speed\nThe LoRA loader also stacks the **viggle turbo 6-step LoRA**, so KSampler runs at **6 steps, cfg 1** for fast swaps. For standard-quality (non-turbo) results, turn that turbo LoRA off and raise steps (~25+).\n\n### Base models\n- [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (~7 GB, default)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf](https://huggingface.co/Abiray/Qwen-Image-2.1-GGUF/tree/main) (or another quant) -> `models/unet/` (low VRAM)\n- [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen3vl_8b_w4a8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (extra low-VRAM encoder)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n\nBFS LoRA by **Alissonerdx** (MIT) - he maintains BFS swap LoRAs for many models; this is the current Qwen-Image 2.1 version. Use responsibly - don't swap faces of real people without their consent."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Qwen-Image 2.1 - BFS Character (Head) Swap\n\nThis is the Qwen-Image 2.1 image-edit workflow set up for **BFS - Best Face Swap** by **Alissonerdx**. Load a **body/base image** (image_1) and a **head/face reference** (image_2), and the LoRA transfers the face and hair from image_2 onto the person in image_1 far more consistently than a plain edit prompt.\n\nNothing extra is needed to use it in your own workflow: just load a BFS LoRA in the LoRA loader and use the swap prompt below.\n\n### BFS LoRA (pick one - try both)\nTwo head-swap LoRAs for Qwen 2.1. v1.1 alternative is the more recent one and is marked recommended, but results vary by image - test both:\n- [bfs_head_v1.1_alternative_qwen_2.1.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Alissonerdx/BFS-Best-Face-Swap/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (loaded here)\n- [bfs_head_v1_qwen_2.1.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Alissonerdx/BFS-Best-Face-Swap/tree/main) -> `models/loras/`\n\nStart at LoRA **strength 1.0**, then adjust for your base model, resolution, and reference image. Input order matters: **body first (image_1), face reference second (image_2).**\n\n### Swap prompt (in the text encode node)\n`head_swap: start with <image1> as the base image, keeping its lighting, environment, and background. remove the head from <image1> completely and replace it with the head from <image2>, strictly preserving the hair, eye color, nose structure from <image2>. copy the direction of the eye, head rotation, micro expressions from <image1>, high quality, sharp details, 4k`\n\n### IMPORTANT - Qwen 2.1 caveat (from the author)\n\"There's a really annoying effect in Qwen 2.1 where even if you change a small part of the image, it seems like the whole image is affected; the colors change, the details are lost, it looks more blurry, etc. The way I managed to mitigate it a bit was by generating the images in 2K, and even then it's still bad.\"\nSo this workflow runs the ResolutionSelector at **2 MP (2K)** to reduce that whole-image drift. Keep it at 2K for the best preservation.\n\n### About this workflow's speed\nThe LoRA loader also stacks the **viggle turbo 6-step LoRA**, so KSampler runs at **6 steps, cfg 1** for fast swaps. For standard-quality (non-turbo) results, turn that turbo LoRA off and raise steps (~25+).\n\n### Base models\n- [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (~7 GB, default)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf](https://huggingface.co/Abiray/Qwen-Image-2.1-GGUF/tree/main) (or another quant) -> `models/unet/` (low VRAM)\n- [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen3vl_8b_w4a8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (extra low-VRAM encoder)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n\nBFS LoRA by **Alissonerdx** (MIT) - he maintains BFS swap LoRAs for many models; this is the current Qwen-Image 2.1 version. Use responsibly - don't swap faces of real people without their consent."
